\begin{example}\label{coxa}
The distance transitive 28-vertex Coxeter graph $Cox$ with intersection array $\{3,2,2,1;1,1,1,2\}$ is shown on the left of Figure~\ref{coxk33} with a TC $\mu$, where a listing is shown, namely $0(6+11=17)$ ,for $i=0,3$, and $i(8+10)=18$, for $i=1,2$.  We resume this by writing $Cox(|Cox^0|,|Cox^1|,|Cox^2|,|Cox^3|)=Cox(17,18,18,17)=Cox(17^218^2)$.
