The first 102-vertex distribution is not yet acceptable: exact equitable DSATUR found witnesses on some seeds within the one-million-node budget, despite other seeds exhausting it. I’m treating that as a real G6 failure, not hiding it behind worst-case NP-completeness. I’m testing the remaining fixed-length axes—class imbalance and additional colour-safe mixing—before deciding whether the answer-size cap forces a documented rejection.
